# Xiaomi Focus Pen Pro - HID keyboard interface
#   bus 0x0005 (Bluetooth), vendor 0x0022, product 0x5081
#
# The pen exposes its gestures as ordinary key usages on its keyboard
# collection. Verified against stock HyperOS 3 (uke, OS3.0.303.0.WOZMIXN)
# by replaying each scan code through /dev/input/event18 and reading the
# key code Android actually delivered:
#
#   gesture        scanCode  stock Generic.kl   delivered to apps
#   pinch            189     F19                194  KEYCODE_BUTTON_7
#   double press      96     NUMPAD_ENTER       195  KEYCODE_BUTTON_8
#   swipe up          73     NUMPAD_9           196  KEYCODE_BUTTON_9
#   swipe down        81     NUMPAD_3           197  KEYCODE_BUTTON_10
#
# Stock does this remap inside its own input stack. Reproducing it here is
# what lets drawing apps such as ONYX StarNote tell the gestures apart:
# pinch and double press arrive as two different button codes, and because
# BUTTON_7..10 carry no character (see the matching .kcm) nothing is typed
# into the canvas either.
#
# Every other scan code keeps the exact Generic.kl behaviour, so nothing
# else about this device changes.

# --- pen gestures -> gamepad button range (stock parity) ---
key 189   BUTTON_7
key 96    BUTTON_8
key 73    BUTTON_9
key 81    BUTTON_10

# --- everything else: identical to Generic.kl ---
key 55    NUMPAD_MULTIPLY
key 69    NUM_LOCK
key 71    NUMPAD_7
key 72    NUMPAD_8
key 74    NUMPAD_SUBTRACT
key 75    NUMPAD_4
key 76    NUMPAD_5
key 77    NUMPAD_6
key 78    NUMPAD_ADD
key 79    NUMPAD_1
key 80    NUMPAD_2
key 82    NUMPAD_0
key 83    NUMPAD_DOT
key 86    BACKSLASH
key 98    NUMPAD_DIVIDE
key 103   DPAD_UP
key 104   PAGE_UP
key 105   DPAD_LEFT
key 106   DPAD_RIGHT
key 107   MOVE_END
key 108   DPAD_DOWN
key 109   PAGE_DOWN
key 111   FORWARD_DEL
key 116   POWER
key 117   NUMPAD_EQUALS
key 127   MENU
key 183   F13
key 184   F14
key 185   F15
key 186   F16
key 187   F17
key 188   F18
